- If both **LocalSubnet** and **RemoteSubnet** are set to specific CIDR blocks, the interested traffic mode is used.', example='10.2.1.0/24,10.2.2.0/24', position='Query'),
  resourceOwnerAccount?: string(name='ResourceOwnerAccount', position='Query'),
  resourceOwnerId?: long(name='ResourceOwnerId', position='Query'),
  tunnelOptionsSpecification?: [ 
    {
      customerGatewayId?: string(name='CustomerGatewayId', description='The instance ID of the customer gateway instance associated with the tunnel.', example='cgw-1nmwbpgrp7ssqm1yn****'),
      enableDpd?: boolean(name='EnableDpd', description='Specifies whether to enable the dead peer detection (DPD) feature for the tunnel. Valid values:

- **true**: Enables the DPD feature. The IPsec initiator sends DPD packets to check whether the peer device is alive. If no correct response is received within the specified time, the peer is considered disconnected. IPsec deletes the ISAKMP SA and the corresponding IPsec SA, and the secure tunnel is also deleted.

- **false**: Disables the DPD feature. The IPsec initiator does not send DPD probe packets.', example='true'),
      enableNatTraversal?: boolean(name='EnableNatTraversal', description='Specifies whether to enable the NAT traversal feature for the tunnel. Valid values:

